{"title":"Factor Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In algebra, the <b>Factor theorem</b> is a theorem regarding the relationships between the factors of a polynomial and its roots.\n</p><p><br />\nOne of it's most important applications is if you are given that a polynomial have certain roots, you will know certain linear factors of the polynomial. Thus, you can test if a linear factor is a factor of a polynomial without using polynomial division and instead plugging in numbers. Conversely, you can determine whether a number in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1acc6639de4f1c620680bec4adf3e668f4db723f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is constant, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is polynomial) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> using polynomial division rather than plugging in large values.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Factor Theorem</b> says that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomial</a>, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b2b7ab0341df3dd3ea02ee6680ae31a947af07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-a$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor\" title=\"Factor\">factor</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d046d648fd236896020419d7cdd75bd0685093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b91a6fd8ad4e6623be629da4efe2437d20c44e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - a$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d077d01694dc31ffa0348dfdd7323746399d469d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = (x - a)Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67abeb8b62ca55a525a8aa23a4fdb79eef199355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\deg(Q(x)) = \\deg(P(x)) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d94cb9bcede29488240b0c2eed89b33cb1d6bf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a) = (a - a)Q(a) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2786f215cc4983bde59e669f40803a6495efd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Apply <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Remainder Theorem\">Remainder Theorem</a> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/323ddccecabe4e45db1fde15634980cfa7e282ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = (x - a)Q(x) + R(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67abeb8b62ca55a525a8aa23a4fdb79eef199355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\deg(Q(x)) = \\deg(P(x)) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eeefa367883375994fd2e1f575d088bce9d8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> is the remainder polynomial such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57a2e3c630547bb8015b058c0d2909488601942c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le\\deg(R(x)) &lt; \\deg(x - a) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eeefa367883375994fd2e1f575d088bce9d8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> can be at most a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constant</a> polynomial.\n</p><p>Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77ba6189a32e5ead2cbb44585ede2285792545c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"10\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154c07a6113dd26e28954e4b8287614d58995a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a) = (a - a)Q(a) + R(a) = 0\\Rightarrow R(a) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eeefa367883375994fd2e1f575d088bce9d8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> is a  constant polynomial, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d5586b115b7dc90c675320b3c1f7a4af7f8cc070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d077d01694dc31ffa0348dfdd7323746399d469d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = (x - a)Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, which shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b91a6fd8ad4e6623be629da4efe2437d20c44e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - a$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here are some problems that can be solved using the Factor Theorem:\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5c9c8769cc96ff57b304a20e89f0763a9f06fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000000010$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />-degree polynomial. The Fundamental Theorem of Algebra tells us that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5c9c8769cc96ff57b304a20e89f0763a9f06fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000000010$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> roots, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b52031e22166b450bf6fef6cd514ccbda39439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, \\cdots, r_{10000000010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"13\" />. Suppose all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> ranging from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1af1e63d07e5b51298f8f4b73d4e0e5f03c30e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000000008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639d19f96e7aa389ed47ed3164ed7979e1e1c9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Also, suppose that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e45a6245e10962e00a15248fea1af6963bd099.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2+r_1)(2+r_2) \\cdots (2+r_{10000000010})=m!\\]\" width=\"319\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>for an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the minimum possible positive integral value of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c6ee3bc61e37b83efb891c0abf4f3ab9a6a77d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+r_1)(1+r_2) \\cdots (1+r_{10000000010})\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Find the number of factors of the prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c2a9165a4883d5ca9c2c32a6ac47a3740fa172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999999937$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. (Source: I made it. Solution <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Problems_Collection#Problem_8\" title=\"Problems Collection\">here</a>)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> denotes a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c0efa59cf43ae9af6aa6db9c74ff752004728b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(k)=\\frac{k}{k+1}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"39\" />for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/44275a8a11379c7182dd511858a417c982837d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,\\cdots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d5acd5b4248d21e2216f12640fc8e538efdc600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>(Source: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">1975 USAMO Problem 3</a>)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomials\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Polynomials\">Polynomials</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Remainder Theorem\">Remainder Theorem</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017143303\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 273/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8555/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.639      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.639      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5732:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017143303 and revision id 280934. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}